(9264,'At the bottom of the page, select the new workflow state under <em>Change to:</em> and click <em>Save</em>.','','none'),
(9265,'Who can configure a workflow?','','none'),
(9266,'Make a plan for the new workflow:','','none'),
(9267,'Decide which workflow states you need; for example, <em>Concept</em>, <em>Review</em>, and <em>Final</em>.','','none'),
(9268,'Decide on the settings for each state:','','none'),
(9269,'<em>Label</em>: the state name','','none'),
(9270,'<em>Published</em>: if checked, when content reaches this state it will be made visible on the site (to users with permission).','','none'),
(9271,'<em>Default revision</em>: if checked, when content reaches this state it will become the default revision of the content; published content is automatically the default revision.','','none'),
(9272,'Decide which state content should be created in.','','none'),
(9273,'Decide on the list of allowed transitions between states. For example, you might want a transition between <em>Concept</em> and <em>Review</em>. Each transition has a label; for example, the Concept to Review transition might be labeled \"Review concept\".','','none'),
(9274,'Click <em>Add workflow</em>.','','none'),
