(10652,'Contact Us','','10.5.7'),
(10653,'Configure the meta tags below.','','10.5.7'),
(10654,'Use tokens to avoid redundant meta data and search engine penalization. For example, a \'keyword\' value of \"example\" will be shown on all content using this configuration, whereas using the [node:field_keywords] automatically inserts the \"keywords\" values from the current entity (node, term, etc).','','10.5.7'),
(10655,'Set to %none to disable inheritance of the parent value and prevent the output of this metatag entirely.','','10.5.7'),
(10656,'The text to display in the title bar of a visitor\'s web browser when they view this page. This meta tag may also be used as the title of the page when a visitor bookmarks or favorites this page, or as the page title in a search engine result. It is common to append \'[site:name]\' to the end of this, so the site\'s name is automatically added. It is recommended that the title is no greater than 55 - 65 characters long, including spaces.','','10.5.7'),
(10657,'A brief and concise summary of the page\'s content that is a maximum of 160 characters in length. The description meta tag may be used by search engines to display a snippet about the page in search results.','','10.5.7'),
(10658,'A brief and concise summary of the page\'s content, preferably 150 characters or less. Where as the description meta tag may be used by search engines to display a snippet about the page in search results, the abstract tag may be used to archive a summary about the page. This meta tag is <em>no longer</em> supported by major search engines.','','10.5.7'),
(10659,'A comma-separated list of keywords about the page. This meta tag is <em>no longer</em> supported by most search engines.','','10.5.7'),
(10660,'A location\'s formal name.','','10.5.7'),
(10661,'A location\'s two-letter international country code, with an optional two-letter region, e.g. \'US-NH\' for New Hampshire in the USA.','','10.5.7'),
(10662,'Geo-spatial information in \'latitude, longitude\' format, e.g. \'50.167958, -97.133185\'; <a href=\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ICBM_address\' aria-label=\'see Wikipedia for details on ICBM addresses\'>see Wikipedia for details</a>.','','10.5.7'),
(10663,'Geo-spatial information in \'latitude; longitude\' format, e.g. \'50.167958; -97.133185\'; <a href=\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geographic_coordinate_system\' aria-label=\'see Wikipedia for details on the geographic coordinate system\'>see Wikipedia for details</a>.','','10.5.7'),
(10664,'A link to the preferred page location or URL of the content of this page, to help eliminate duplicate content penalties from search engines.','','10.5.7'),
(10665,'A brief URL, often created by a URL shortening service.','','10.5.7'),
(10666,'Used for paginated content by providing URL with rel=\'next\' link.','','10.5.7'),
(10667,'Used for paginated content by providing URL with rel=\'prev\' link.','','10.5.7'),
(10668,'Used to indicate the URL that broke the story, and can link to either an internal URL or an external source. If the full URL is not known it is acceptable to use a partial URL or just the domain name.','','10.5.7'),
(10669,'Define the author of a page.','','10.5.7'),
(10670,'Describes the name and version number of the software or publishing tool used to create the page.','','10.5.7'),
(10671,'This will be able to extract the URL from an image field if the field is configured properly.','','10.5.7'),
(10672,'An image associated with this page, for use as a thumbnail in social networks and other services.','','10.5.7'),
(10673,'Used to rate content for audience appropriateness. This tag has little known influence on search engine rankings, but can be used by browsers, browser extensions, and apps. The <a href=\'https://www.metatags.org/meta_name_rating\'>most common options</a> are general, mature, restricted, 14 years, safe for kids. If you follow the <a href=\'https://www.rtalabel.org/index.php?content=howto\'>RTA Documentation</a> you should enter RTA-5042-1996-1400-1577-RTA','','10.5.7'),
(10674,'The number of seconds to wait before refreshing the page. May also force redirect to another page using the format \'5; url=https://example.com/\', which would be triggered after five seconds.','','10.5.7'),
(10675,'<a href=\'https://www.metatags.org/meta_http_equiv_set_cookie\'>Sets a cookie</a> on the visitor\'s browser. Can be in either NAME=VALUE format, or a more verbose format including the path and expiration date; see the link for full details on the syntax.','','10.5.7'),
(10676,'Details about intellectual property, such as copyright or trademarks; does not automatically protect the site\'s content or intellectual property.','','10.5.7'),
(10677,'This meta tag communicates with Google. There are currently two directives supported: \'nositelinkssearchbox\' to not to show the sitelinks search box, and \'notranslate\' to ask Google not to offer a translation of the page. Both options may be added, just separate them with a comma. See <a href=\'https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/79812?hl=en\'>meta tags that Google understands</a> for further details.','','10.5.7'),
(10678,'Tell search engines when to index the page again. Very few search engines support this tag, it is more useful to use an <a href=\'https://www.drupal.org/project/xmlsitemap\'>XML Sitemap</a> file.','','10.5.7'),
(10679,'Used to control whether a browser caches a specific page locally. Not commonly used. Should be used in conjunction with the Pragma meta tag.','','10.5.7'),
(10680,'Control when the browser\'s internal cache of the current page should expire. The date must to be an <a href=\'https://www.csgnetwork.com/timerfc1123calc.html\'>RFC-1123</a>-compliant date string that is represented in Greenwich Mean Time (GMT), e.g. \'Thu, 01 Sep 2016 00:12:56 GMT\'. Set to \'0\' to stop the page being cached entirely.','','10.5.7'),
(10681,'Used to control whether a browser caches a specific page locally. Not commonly used. Should be used in conjunction with the Cache-Control meta tag.','','10.5.7'),
(10682,'Simple meta tags.','','10.5.7'),
(10683,'index - Allow search engines to index this page (assumed).','','10.5.7'),
(10684,'follow - Allow search engines to follow links on this page (assumed).','','10.5.7'),
(10685,'noindex - Prevents search engines from indexing this page.','','10.5.7'),
(10686,'nofollow - Prevents search engines from following links on this page.','','10.5.7'),
(10687,'noarchive - Prevents cached copies of this page from appearing in search results.','','10.5.7'),
(10688,'nosnippet - Prevents descriptions from appearing in search results, and prevents page caching.','','10.5.7'),
(10689,'noimageindex - Prevent search engines from indexing images on this page.','','10.5.7'),
(10690,'notranslate - Prevent search engines from offering to translate this page in search results.','','10.5.7'),
(10691,'Provides search engines with specific directions for what to do when this page is indexed.','','10.5.7'),
(10692,'Max Snippet','','10.5.7'),
(10693,'Use a number character as a textual snippet for this search result. \"0\" equals \"nosnippet\". \"-1\" will let the search engine decide the most effective length.','','10.5.7'),
(10694,'Max Video Preview','','10.5.7'),
(10695,'Use a maximum of number seconds as a video snippet for videos on this page in search results. \"0\" will use a static a image. \"-1\" means there is no limit.','','10.5.7'),
(10696,'None - no image preview is to be shown.','','10.5.7'),
(10697,'Standard - a default image preview may be shown.','','10.5.7'),
(10698,'Large - a larger image preview, up to the width of the viewport, may be shown.','','10.5.7'),
(10699,'Max Image Preview','','10.5.7'),
